Assist in maintenance of aseptic tissue culture conditions and ensuring minimum contamination in cultures;
Report on plantlets of selected yam varieties produced using bar code labeling;
Assist in submission of monthly report and populating the online high ratio propagation database www.yamhrponline.iita.org on the details of seed yam produced including genotype, quantity, age, cycle number and disease status;
Assist in submission of documentation on flow of plantlets to end users monthly;
Assist in daily and weekly report on the functioning of the conventional tissue culture facilities;
Report any malfunction of materials and equipment;
Qualifications
HND/BSc in Agriculture, Biology, Microbiology, Physiology, Biochemistry or related courses with at least two (2) years’ relevant experience performing similar role.
Competencies
Ideal Candidate must:
Have good knowledge of contamination reduction strategies, including cleanliness and familiarity with aseptic and safe tissue culture laboratory practices.
Have good knowledge on use of computer for data reporting;
Be ready to work in a team and have a good sense of interpersonal relationship.
Remuneration
We offer highly competitive salary with equally attractive benefits and excellent working conditions in a pleasant campus environment.
